      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `StagingAllocator` (`python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/common/staging_buffer.py`), `self.alloc_order: List[int]` was maintained alongside `self.allocations: dict` to track the oldest un-freed allocation for watermark updates:\n\n```python\nwhile self.alloc_order and self.alloc_order[0] not in self.allocations:\n    self.alloc_order.pop(0)\n```\n\nBecause `assign()` assigns strictly monotonic `alloc_id`s once at the tail of `self.allocations` and `free()` only deletes entries via `self.allocations.pop(alloc_id)`, Python's insertion-ordered `dict` already preserves the exact chronological order of all live allocations:\n1. With `self.alloc_order: List[int]`, every in-order `free()` performed an $O(N)$ `list.pop(0)` shift while holding `self.lock`.\n2. Worse, when disaggregated KV transfers completed out of order while an older allocation remained in flight, freed `alloc_id` tombstones stayed inside `self.alloc_order` until the head allocation finished, at which point `free()` executed a tight loop of $K$ consecutive `list.pop(0)` shifts ($O(K^2)$ time under `self.lock`).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Remove the redundant `self.alloc_order` list in `StagingAllocator`.\n- Read the oldest live allocation directly via `next(iter(self.allocations.values()))` in $O(1)$ worst-case time and $O(\\text{active allocations})$ space.\n- Add `test_out_of_order_frees_advance_watermark_to_oldest_live_allocation` in `test/registered/unit/disaggregation/test_disaggregation_wire.py`.\n\n## Accuracy & Verification\n\n```bash\npytest -q test/registered/unit/disaggregation/test_disaggregation_wire.py -k \"TestStagingWatermark or TestStagingScatterLifecycle\"\n# 5 passed\n```\n\n## Acknowledgements\n\nCredit to `@YAMY1234` (#37166), `@ShangmingCai` (#47652), `@kpjeeja` (#40861), and `@kpham-sgl` (#35762) for the surrounding `StagingAllocator` ring buffer design and lifecycle tests.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41603774072](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41603774072)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41603773856](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41603773856)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41603773870](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41603773870)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
